        "original_id": "87a12424-7f59-556d-94be-916072bbdf08",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1932 Allan Cup, 1933 World Ice Hockey Championships\n- Places: Prague, Czechoslovakia\n- Countries: Canada, United States\n- Topics: Overtime in ice hockey, shootout\n\nFacts:\n- The team from the 1932 Allan Cup went on to represent Canada at the 1933 World Ice Hockey Championships in Prague, Czechoslovakia.\n- At the 1933 World Ice Hockey Championships, Canada lost the final game to the United States in overtime and won the silver medal.\n- In ice hockey, two main methods of extending a game are the overtime period, commonly called overtime, and the shootout.",
